{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and transformer aggregation is the strongest baseline (config_006, acc 0.653, F1 0.628), slightly ahead of avgpool and much ahead of pca or scgpt variants. Image-only ResNet is weak (config_011, acc 0.328), so the key uncertainty is whether adding image features to the best RNA representation improves validation accuracy. config_032 extends config_006 by adding the already-baselined ResNet image encoder with simple concat fusion while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed. This directly tests the contribution of the image modality relative to the best RNA-only model and is a focused, high-value next step before testing more complex fusion or stronger image encoders."
}

